it (born 8 June 1972), also known as \"Roozey\" or \"Skerro\", is a Dominican politician who has been Prime Minister of Dominica since 2004; he has also been the Member of Parliament for the Vieille Case constituency since 2000. Regionally, he has served as the chairman of the Organisation of Eastern Caribbean States (OECS) and, most recently, as chairman of the Caribbean Community (CARICOM) in 2010 and 2023. Skerrit is currently the longest-serving prime minister of Dominica, and, since the ousting of Ralph Gonsalves in November 2025, he has been the longest-serving democratic leader.","image":"RooseveltSkerrit.jpg","birth":1972.4344262295083,"death":null},"Q1707507":{"label":"Eliud Williams","description":"President of Dominica","enwiki":"Eliud Williams","summary":"Eliud Thaddeus Williams (born 21 August 1948) is a Dominican politician who  served as seventh President of Dominica from 2012 to 2013.","image":null,"birth":1948.636612021858,"death":null},"Q2960197":{"label":"Charles Savarin","description":"President of Dominica (2013–2023)","enwiki":"Charles Savarin","summary":"Charles Angelo Savarin, DAH (born 2 October 1943) is a politician from Dominica who served as President of Dominica from 2013 to 2023. He is a member of the Dominica Labour Party and served for a time as Minister for National Security, Immigration, Labour and the Public Service.","image":"Savarin entering (cropped).jpg","birth":1943.7506849315068,"death":null},"Q310129":{"label":"Nicholas Liverpool","description":"President of Dominica (1934-2015)","enwiki":"Nicholas Liverpool","summary":"Nicholas Joseph Orville Liverpool (9 September 1934 – 1 June 2015) was a politician and jurist from Dominica who served as the sixth President of Dominica from 2 October 2003 to 17 September 2012.","image":"Nicholas Liverpool.jpg","birth":1934.6876712328767,"death":2015.4136986301369},"Q887688":{"label":"Vernon Shaw","description":"President of Dominica (1930-2013)","enwiki":"Vernon Shaw","summary":"Vernon Lorden Shaw (13 May 1930 – 2 December 2013) was the fifth President of Dominica, in office from 1998 to 2003.\nShaw was an alumnus of the Dominica Grammar School and Trinity College, Oxford. He was a career civil servant, rising to the post of Cabinet Secretary in 1977, and retiring in 1990. He became resident tutor of the University of the West Indies in 1991.","image":"Vernon Shaw (crop2).jpg","birth":1930.3616438356164,"death":2013.9178082191781}},"media":{"Flag of Dominica.svg":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Flag_of_Dominica.svg/330px-Flag_of_Dominica.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Dominica.svg","author":"Alwin Bully","license":"Public domain"},"Coat of arms of Dominica.svg":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/Coat_of_arms_of_Dominica.svg/330px-Coat_of_arms_of_Dominica.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coat_of_arms_of_Dominica.svg","author":"See File History, below, for details.","license":"Attribution"},"Sylvanie Burton (cropped).jpg":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Sylvanie_Burton_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Sylvanie_Burton_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sylvanie_Burton_(cropped).jpg","author":"U.S. Embassy Bridgetown","license":"Public domain"},"RooseveltSkerrit.jpg":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/RooseveltSkerrit.jpg/330px-RooseveltSkerrit.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:RooseveltSkerrit.jpg","author":"[mjones]","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0"},"Savarin entering (cropped).jpg":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/com